    ["Mesh-检视用南瓜"] = "Сетка - Тыква для осмотра",
    ["People these days will do anything against their conscience for profit. May the Earth Mother bless you with health, {{先生|女士}}."] = "В наши дни люди ради выгоды сделают все против своей совести. Да благословит тебя Мать-Земля здоровьем, {{Sir|Madam}}.",
    ["—In that parallel world, Audrey and Susie worked together to solve the case involving Fors's companion. \n\n      Backlund, the Hall family garden. Audrey sat on a hanging chair, sunlight casting dappled light and shadows through the vines. \n      A few days ago, the expression on Fors Wall's face when she visited appeared in her mind again. That lazy-tempered writer had shown a solemn look: \"I have a companion who has been thrown into prison and is waiting for the final verdict. I hope you can save her, no matter what method you use.\" \n      And the accompanying Viscount Glaint had sent someone to consult a well-known lawyer, who said there was a chance for a light sentence, but an acquittal was very difficult unless the defendant could obtain a medical certificate stating they had mental issues or were mentally underdeveloped... \n      Audrey remembered that she had promised Fors she would consider it carefully. When the writer left, she had looked back, anticipation hidden in her light blue eyes. \n      \"Medical certificate...\" Audrey whispered to herself, her brows slightly furrowed. It wasn't that she hadn't thought about using the Hall family's influence to pull strings, but that would expose her relationship with Fors and Xio. Moreover, although the gang leader had issued a statement of forgiveness, the case of grievous injury could still be prosecuted. \n      Susie, lying beside her, pricked up her ears and whispered in a voice only Audrey could hear: \"That gang leader, is he still in the hospital?\" \n      Audrey looked down at her, her gaze flickering. \n      \"I'll go give it a try,\" Susie suggested, wagging her tail. \n      That night, Susie quietly snuck into the hospital room. She used her Spectator ability to gently guide the \"decent gentleman\" to recall—the other party finally remembered that he had struck first and that Xio was only acting in self-defense. After waking up, he took the initiative to correct his testimony to the prosecutor. \n      A few days later, Xio was acquitted. When Fors came to the Hall residence to thank her, she sighed, \"The prosecutor suddenly found new evidence; what good luck.\" \n      Audrey smiled and nodded: \"Yes, what good luck.\" \n      Susie lay at her feet, her tail thumping against the carpet, feeling satisfied."] = "—In that parallel world, Audrey and Susie worked together to solve the case involving Fors's companion. \n\n      Бэкланд, the Hall family garden. Audrey sat on a hanging chair, sunlight casting dappled light and shadows through the vines. \n      A few days ago, the expression on Fors Wall's face when she visited appeared in her mind again. That lazy-tempered writer had shown a solemn look: \"I have a companion who has been thrown into prison and is waiting for the final verdict. I hope you can save her, no matter what method you use.\" \n      And the accompanying Viscount Glaint had sent someone to consult a well-known lawyer, who said there was a chance for a light sentence, but an acquittal was very difficult unless the defendant could obtain a medical certificate stating they had mental issues or were mentally underdeveloped... \n      Audrey remembered that she had promised Fors she would consider it carefully. When the writer left, she had looked back, anticipation hidden in her light blue eyes. \n      \"Medical certificate...\" Audrey whispered to herself, her brows slightly furrowed. It wasn't that she hadn't thought about using the Hall family's influence to pull strings, but that would expose her relationship with Fors and Xio. Moreover, although the gang leader had issued a statement of forgiveness, the case of grievous injury could still be prosecuted. \n      Susie, lying beside her, pricked up her ears and whispered in a voice only Audrey could hear: \"That gang leader, is he still in the hospital?\" \n      Audrey looked down at her, her gaze flickering. \n      \"I'll go give it a try,\" Susie suggested, wagging her tail. \n      That night, Susie quietly snuck into the hospital room. She used her Зритель ability to gently guide the \"decent gentleman\" to recall—the other party finally remembered that he had struck first and that Xio was only acting in self-defense. After waking up, he took the initiative to correct his testimony to the prosecutor. \n      A few days later, Xio was acquitted. When Fors came to the Hall residence to thank her, she sighed, \"The prosecutor suddenly found new evidence; what good luck.\" \n      Audrey smiled and nodded: \"Yes, what good luck.\" \n      Susie lay at her feet, her tail thumping against the carpet, feeling satisfied.",
